course: dictionary
lesson: 14735
title: Prolong: making things last longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To prolong something means to make it last longer. Look for the word long hiding inside it, and you have a clue. «We did not want the holiday to end, so we tried to prolong it by staying one more week.» The holiday was made to last longer, so prolong means to stretch time out.
explain: The words around it give you more clues. «The rain was prolonged, falling for three whole days.» Prolonged describes rain that went on for a long time. To check, swap in make it last longer: three whole days of rain that lasted longer still makes sense.
explain: Prolong can also be about life and health. «The new medicine may prolong his life.» This means the medicine could help him live longer. Scientists use the word too: keeping food in a fridge prolongs how fresh it stays.
fact: Prolong means to make something last longer.
fact: Prolong is a verb, so its forms are prolongs, prolonged and prolonging.
fact: «Prolong the agony» means to make a painful or unpleasant time last longer.
fact: «Prolonged» means long-lasting, as in «prolonged rain».
fact: A good check is to swap in make it last longer and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «We asked Dad to prolong our game of tag before bedtime.» What does prolong mean? | Make it end quickly | *Make it last longer | Make it wetter | Make it louder
exercise: «The bus was late, and the wait at the stop was prolonged.» What does prolonged suggest? | Quick and short | *Long-lasting, going on for a long time | Sudden and surprising | Blue and shiny
exercise: Which word means to make something last longer? | sudden | bright | quiet | *prolong
test: «Keeping the bread in the freezer will prolong how long it stays fresh.» What does prolong mean? | Make it wet | Make it end sooner | *Make it last longer | Make it smaller
test: Which word is the best swap for prolong in «The treatment helped prolong her life»? | Shorten | Forget | Repeat | *Lengthen
exam: Mia says, «The rain was prolonged.» What does prolonged mean? | Short and sharp | *Long-lasting | Bright and sunny | Invisible
